{#
  One URL, generated.

  The hand-maintained sitemap listed seven: the root plus six #anchors, out of
  seventeen projects, all stamped 2024-12-20. It had drifted twice over —
  missing eleven projects added since, and dated to a day the content no longer
  matched.

  It is not worth listing anchors at all. Search engines canonicalise a URL
  fragment to the page it sits on, so seventeen #project entries index as one
  page regardless; the only thing the extra entries could do is go stale, which
  is exactly what they did. One accurate entry beats seventeen approximate ones.

  lastmod comes from the build, so it is right by construction rather than by
  someone remembering.
#}
<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<urlset xmlns="http://www.sitemaps.org/schemas/sitemap/0.9">
  <url>
    <loc>https://rosehallgren.se/</loc>
    <lastmod>{{ page.date | isoDate }}</lastmod>
    <changefreq>monthly</changefreq>
    <priority>1.0</priority>
  </url>
</urlset>
